  "details": "There appears to be a state where the local player position and the networked/collision-authoritative position diverge while a menu is open.\n\nObserved symptoms:\n\nThe player's nameplate remains at the position where the menu was opened, while the local view continues to move\n\nWorld colliders do not block movement in this state, allowing entry into areas that are otherwise geometrically inaccessible\n\nImpact: this defeats any world-side access control that relies on physical geometry. Backstage areas at events, gated content, and puzzle/escape room worlds all depend on walls actually being walls. It also breaks Udon logic that uses trigger colliders to gate progression, since a player can reach a downstream trigger without passing the upstream ones.\n\nI'm not including reproduction steps in this message. I can provide them, along with video, on request through whichever channel you prefer.",
